/-!
# Prime-exponent pole kernel compatibility

The prime-exponent factor carrier generates an actual quarter-test orbit from
the same modified-WeakFE source test used by the complete pole energy.  Both
the complete-orbit positive energy and the Mellin read are factored through
that test orbit.  The existing quarter-test kernel theorem then rules out an
energy-zero/Mellin-nonzero factor event without boundedness or critical-line
premises.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 3000000

